<title>FRANCE: Paris airports' import cargo up 4.8pct in March 97.</title>
<headline>Paris airports' import cargo up 4.8pct in March 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>March 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 50,878 tonnes, an increase of 4.8 percent on the same month the previous year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Global ADP import traffic in March 1997, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on March 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>Domestic	  2,180	     down 18.9 percent</p>
<p>European Union  6,180		 up 19.7</p>
<p>Non-EU Europe   1,088		  up 1.5</p>
<p>North Africa    1,096	     down 26.0</p>
<p>Sub-Saharan Africa</p>
<p>		    5,234		down 0.3</p>
<p>North America  16,417		down 3.1</p>
<p>French territories</p>
<p>		    1,827		  up 3.8</p>
<p>Latin America   2,271		 up 15.7</p>
<p>Middle East     2,294		down 3.2</p>
<p>Far East	 12,291		 up 24.8</p>
<p>Total	    50,878		  up 4.8</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
